//! The `text-decoration-inset` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property
//! enables adjusting the start and end points of an element's text decoration so it can be
//! shortened, lengthened, or have its position shifted with respect to the rendered text.
//!
//! Initial: 0. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: refer to the size of the box itself.
//!
//! Grammar: <length-percentage>{1,2} | auto
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-decor-4/#propdef-text-decoration-inset
//!
//! Author guide:
